WEBVTT

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.924
As new employees,
I'd like your opinion on our commercial.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.551
I've paid to have it aired
during the Super Bowl.

00:00:09.635 --> 00:00:12.596
- Wow.
- Not on the same channel, of course.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:18.060
Interplanetary deliveries...
What a headache.

00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:20.562
Evans, where is that package from earth?

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.688
Uh...

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:25.901
I'm not Evans!

00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:28.403
He should have used Planet Express.

00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:33.158
When those other companies
aren't brave or foolhardy enough to go,

00:00:33.242 --> 00:00:36.286
trust Planet Express
for reliable, on-time delivery.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:42.793
Here's your package,
Mr. Horrible Gelatinous Blob.

00:00:42.918 --> 00:00:46.505
Good work, Evans.
You've got a future around here.

00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:51.426
Thank you, sir.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.054
Planet Express.
Our crew is replaceable,

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:55.681
your package isn't.

00:00:57.683 --> 00:00:59.476
Are there really giant birds like that?

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.688
No, no, that was all
just special effects.

00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:04.565
Now, let's have breakfast.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.859
I hope everyone likes eggs.

00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:54.072
I'm never going to get used
to the 31st century.

00:01:54.239 --> 00:01:55.574
Caffeinated bacon?

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:57.534
Baconated grapefruit?

00:01:57.910 --> 00:01:59.244
Admiral Crunch?

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:02.414
Well, if you don't like that
try some Archduke Chocula.

00:02:03.415 --> 00:02:04.875
Ah, Hermes.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.252
Crew, meet Hermes Conrad.

00:02:07.336 --> 00:02:09.546
He manages my delivery business.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:13.091
Pays the bills,
notifies next of kin, what have you.

00:02:13.217 --> 00:02:15.886
Someone come and drop this package
through the slot last night.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.596
Now, which one of you
is the captain?

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:20.724
Oh, my. I haven't picked
a new captain yet.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:23.268
It's always so hard to choose.

00:02:23.602 --> 00:02:25.354
Ooh. Ooh, ooh, ooh!

00:02:28.357 --> 00:02:30.192
Mmm... You.

00:02:32.361 --> 00:02:36.198
Okay, Captain,
this is just a standard legal release

00:02:36.281 --> 00:02:39.535
protecting Planet Express from lawsuits
in the event of the unforeseen.

00:02:39.743 --> 00:02:41.578
- "Death by airlock failure."
- Mm-hmm.

00:02:41.662 --> 00:02:43.664
- "Death by brain parasite."
- Ya.

00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:45.290
"Death by sonic diarrhea."

00:02:45.374 --> 00:02:46.500
Oh, you don't want that.

00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:49.002
Look, I don't know
about your previous captains,

00:02:49.086 --> 00:02:51.463
but I intend to do
as little dying as possible.

00:02:53.715 --> 00:02:54.800
Sign the paper.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.678
And now, Fry,
before you go into space

00:02:57.761 --> 00:03:00.055
you'll need to see our staff doctor.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:04.142
I should warn you, though,
he's a little unusual.

00:03:04.393 --> 00:03:05.853
He wears sandals.

00:03:09.982 --> 00:03:13.610
Dr. Zoidberg, this is Fry,
the new delivery boy.

00:03:13.694 --> 00:03:14.903
He needs a physical.

00:03:14.987 --> 00:03:16.655
Excellent, excellent.

00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:20.951
You'll be fine.

00:03:23.537 --> 00:03:26.623
Now, open your mouth
and let's have a look at that brain.

00:03:26.707 --> 00:03:28.917
No, no, no, not that mouth.

00:03:29.001 --> 00:03:30.294
I only have one.

00:03:30.544 --> 00:03:31.712
Really?

00:03:32.337 --> 00:03:34.840
Uh... Is there a human doctor around?

00:03:34.965 --> 00:03:37.426
Young lady, I'm an expert on humans.

00:03:37.509 --> 00:03:39.887
Now pick a mouth, open it, and say...

00:03:41.388 --> 00:03:42.389
Uh...

00:03:43.807 --> 00:03:46.185
What? My mother was a saint!

00:03:46.268 --> 00:03:47.394
Get out!

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.321
Dear Lord, Bender, you're filthy.

00:03:57.654 --> 00:04:00.282
Yeah, like you don't
have crap in your neck.

00:04:00.532 --> 00:04:02.451
Amy, why don't you give his body

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:04.244
a going-over with the cleaning pick?

00:04:04.328 --> 00:04:05.454
Okay.

00:04:05.537 --> 00:04:07.497
Does it hurt when I go like this?

00:04:07.581 --> 00:04:08.624
Ow!

00:04:08.749 --> 00:04:09.791
A little.

00:04:10.042 --> 00:04:12.503
Well, the doctor says
I'm as healthy as a crab.

00:04:12.586 --> 00:04:13.837
Can I go into space now?

00:04:13.921 --> 00:04:16.048
As soon as we finish cleaning Bender.

00:04:16.131 --> 00:04:17.216
Oh, and Fry...

00:04:17.299 --> 00:04:19.760
This is our intern, Amy Wong.

00:04:19.843 --> 00:04:21.762
She's an engineering student of mine.

00:04:21.929 --> 00:04:23.305
I like having her around

00:04:23.388 --> 00:04:25.432
because she has
the same blood type as me.

00:04:25.766 --> 00:04:30.062
Hey, you're the unfrozen guy
from the 20th century, right?

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.813
Last time I checked.

00:04:32.064 --> 00:04:35.108
Hang on. Amy Wong, of the Mars Wongs?

00:04:35.192 --> 00:04:37.319
Look, we're not as rich as everybody says.

00:04:37.402 --> 00:04:40.239
Uh-huh. What sorority do you belong to?

00:04:40.771 --> 00:04:41.848
Kappa Kappa Wong.

00:04:41.932 --> 00:04:43.016
Hey, rich girl!

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.143
Look over here.
It's me, Bender.

00:04:45.227 --> 00:04:46.895
I'm being entertaining.

00:04:46.978 --> 00:04:49.022
La-la-la, look at my head

00:04:49.106 --> 00:04:51.316
It's okay to look at my head

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:54.027
I got a big ol' head
And hey! Ho!

00:04:54.444 --> 00:04:56.238
All right, show's over. I'm tired.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.490
Ah, to be young again...

00:04:58.573 --> 00:05:00.075
And also a robot.

00:05:00.325 --> 00:05:01.535
Oh! Now, as I recall,

00:05:01.618 --> 00:05:03.704
you youngsters
have a package to deliver.

00:05:03.787 --> 00:05:06.915
Finally. Come on, Bender.
Let's mosey.

00:05:09.918 --> 00:05:11.294
Nice catch, idiot.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.427
So, where are we going anyway?

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.137
Nowhere special, the moon.

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:21.346
The moo... The moon?

00:05:21.371 --> 00:05:22.372
The moon moon?

00:05:22.541 --> 00:05:25.878
Wow, I'm going to be a famous hero
just like Neil Armstrong

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:28.437
and those other brave guys
no one ever heard of.

00:05:28.645 --> 00:05:30.814
Oh! I love stuff like the moon.

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:31.982
Can I come, Leela?

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:34.609
Well... I guess so.

00:05:34.693 --> 00:05:35.819
Just be careful.

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:37.738
I'd like to hold off
any major screw-ups

00:05:37.821 --> 00:05:39.906
until at least
my second day as captain.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:41.908
Nothing will go wrong.

00:05:41.992 --> 00:05:44.202
If something goes wrong
bring back the blood.

00:05:52.269 --> 00:05:53.270
Can I do the countdown?

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:54.563
Huh? Oh, sure.

00:05:54.646 --> 00:05:55.731
Knock yourself out.

00:05:55.814 --> 00:05:57.608
Ten, nine...

00:05:57.691 --> 00:05:58.984
Okay, we're here.

00:05:59.151 --> 00:06:01.236
...eight, seven, six, five,
four, three, two, one. Blastoff.

00:06:10.704 --> 00:06:12.289
Hurry up.
I want to see the moon.

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:14.583
Relax, it's open till 9:00.

00:06:15.042 --> 00:06:17.794
That's one small step for Fry...

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:20.672
And one giant line for admission.

00:06:21.632 --> 00:06:23.759
Wow!

00:06:23.884 --> 00:06:25.552
Um... Can I have cuts?

00:06:25.636 --> 00:06:27.930
Hmm... Mmm...

00:06:28.138 --> 00:06:29.306
No!

00:06:33.894 --> 00:06:35.395
You're not going to believe this,

00:06:35.479 --> 00:06:37.773
but they landed
an amusement park on the moon.

00:06:37.898 --> 00:06:40.734
Guh! It's the happiest place
orbiting earth.

00:06:40.817 --> 00:06:42.152
Let's go already.

00:06:42.236 --> 00:06:44.196
Fry, we have a crate to deliver.

00:06:44.321 --> 00:06:47.074
Let's just dump it in the sewer
and say we delivered it.

00:06:47.157 --> 00:06:48.200
Too much work.

00:06:48.283 --> 00:06:50.577
Let's burn it and say
we dumped it in the sewer.

00:06:50.744 --> 00:06:53.622
Okay, if everyone's finished
being stupid...

00:06:53.705 --> 00:06:55.499
I had more, but you go ahead.

00:06:55.582 --> 00:06:57.543
We'll deliver that crate
like professionals

00:06:57.626 --> 00:06:58.877
and then we'll go home.

00:06:59.086 --> 00:07:01.129
But I've never been
to the moon before.

00:07:01.672 --> 00:07:03.382
Oh, all right.

00:07:03.465 --> 00:07:05.634
We'll deliver that crate
like professionals

00:07:05.717 --> 00:07:07.845
And then we'll go
ride the bumper cars.

00:07:10.138 --> 00:07:12.724
Amy, why don't you help Fry
hoist down the crate?

00:07:12.975 --> 00:07:14.309
Then lock up when you're done.

00:07:14.393 --> 00:07:15.769
Just be careful.

00:07:15.853 --> 00:07:18.480
Aye, aye, Captain.
I mean, only one eye.

00:07:18.772 --> 00:07:20.732
I mean, yes, sir... um, ma'am.

00:07:21.567 --> 00:07:23.151
- Clear?
- Clear.

00:07:23.235 --> 00:07:25.028
- Ready to hoist?
- Ready.

00:07:26.572 --> 00:07:27.698
Ow!

00:07:35.372 --> 00:07:37.291
My first space delivery.

00:07:37.583 --> 00:07:39.251
Greetings, moon man.

00:07:39.334 --> 00:07:40.502
We come in peace.

00:07:40.836 --> 00:07:43.005
I am Fry, from the planet Earth.

00:07:43.297 --> 00:07:44.464
Wise guy, huh?

00:07:44.715 --> 00:07:47.301
If I wasn't so lazy
I'd punch you in the stomach.

00:07:47.509 --> 00:07:48.886
But you are lazy, right?

00:07:49.052 --> 00:07:50.888
Oh, don't get me started.

00:08:04.443 --> 00:08:06.778
Hi! I'm Craterface.

00:08:06.862 --> 00:08:08.697
Welcome to Luna Park.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.366
I'll have to confiscate
your alcohol, sir.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:14.161
Better mascots than you have tried.

00:08:17.664 --> 00:08:20.375
At least I still have my self-respect.

00:08:31.428 --> 00:08:33.972
Ugh, who buys this trash?

00:08:34.181 --> 00:08:37.059
Idiots who need gifts for other idiots.

00:08:37.142 --> 00:08:39.520
Hey, I got you guys
refrigerator magnets.

00:08:42.189 --> 00:08:43.440
Get it off. Get it off!

00:08:43.524 --> 00:08:44.566
Get it... Uh-oh.

00:08:45.108 --> 00:08:49.321
How many roads
must a man walk down

00:08:49.404 --> 00:08:51.114
Before you...

00:08:56.411 --> 00:08:58.247
Keep those things off of me.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:00.791
Magnets screw up my inhibition unit.

00:09:00.999 --> 00:09:04.294
So you flip out and start acting
like some crazy folk singer?

00:09:04.419 --> 00:09:07.631
Yes. I guess a robot
would have to be crazy

00:09:07.714 --> 00:09:09.925
to want to be a folk singer.

00:09:12.553 --> 00:09:16.598
We're whalers on the moon,
we carry a harpoon

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:19.059
But there ain't no whales,
so we tell tall tales

00:09:19.142 --> 00:09:21.311
And sing our whaling tune

00:09:21.395 --> 00:09:23.814
Bender! Hey, Bender! Over here!

00:09:23.897 --> 00:09:27.276
Oh, geez, I went to
high school with that guy.

00:09:27.484 --> 00:09:29.152
Monsanto presents...

00:09:29.236 --> 00:09:31.321
The Goophy Gopher Revue.

00:09:32.114 --> 00:09:35.909
Why does a moon rock
taste better than an earth rock?

00:09:36.034 --> 00:09:38.829
Because it's a little "meteor."

00:09:43.292 --> 00:09:44.501
This is weak.

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:48.005
Address all complaints
to the Monsanto corporation.

00:09:50.883 --> 00:09:52.009
What's wrong, Fry?

00:09:52.092 --> 00:09:53.343
I don't know.

00:09:53.427 --> 00:09:56.263
This place is great and all
but it's just so artificial.

00:09:56.471 --> 00:09:58.932
The gravity, the air, the gophers.

00:09:59.016 --> 00:10:00.392
You might as well stay on earth.

00:10:01.351 --> 00:10:02.895
That's what I came to see.

00:10:04.271 --> 00:10:06.440
I want to go out there
and jump around like an astronaut.

00:10:06.565 --> 00:10:08.108
Screw this phony stuff.

00:10:08.192 --> 00:10:10.235
But the phony stuff is what's fun.

00:10:10.319 --> 00:10:11.486
It's boring out there.

00:10:11.612 --> 00:10:14.448
Yeah. You're the kind of guy
who visits Jerusalem

00:10:14.531 --> 00:10:16.825
and doesn't want to see
the "Sexateria."

00:10:17.242 --> 00:10:20.746
Maybe I should take Fry
on the Lunar Rover Ride.

00:10:20.829 --> 00:10:23.707
You get to wear a space suit
and drive around on the surface

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.918
And the line's short
because it's educational.

00:10:26.126 --> 00:10:28.003
I don't care how educational it is.

00:10:28.086 --> 00:10:29.213
Let's do it!

00:10:29.755 --> 00:10:32.549
Next year in Jerusalem!

00:10:33.634 --> 00:10:34.760
Two adults, please.

00:10:34.843 --> 00:10:38.055
Finally, get ready
for some serious moon action.

00:10:41.058 --> 00:10:43.310
The story of lunar exploration

00:10:43.393 --> 00:10:46.688
started with one man...
A man with a dream.

00:10:47.356 --> 00:10:49.525
One of these days, Alice.

00:10:49.608 --> 00:10:53.737
Bang! Zoom!
Straight to the moon!

00:10:54.196 --> 00:10:57.991
Wow. I never realized
the first astronauts were so fat.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:01.161
That's not an astronaut.
It's a TV comedian.

00:11:01.245 --> 00:11:04.831
He was just using space travel
as a metaphor for beating his wife.

00:11:10.546 --> 00:11:14.258
Wow! I could swear I was
really playing Virtual Skeeball.

00:11:14.341 --> 00:11:16.051
- Hmm?
- Look, it's that crate

00:11:16.134 --> 00:11:17.845
we were going to throw in the sewer.

00:11:21.807 --> 00:11:23.141
The keys to the ship!

00:11:23.517 --> 00:11:25.143
They must have fallen into the crate.

00:11:25.269 --> 00:11:27.688
Leela's going to kill me.

00:11:27.771 --> 00:11:30.482
Nah. She'll probably make me do it.

00:11:30.816 --> 00:11:33.318
Mister, could you please
get those keys out for me?

00:11:33.402 --> 00:11:36.029
What do I look like,
a guy who's not lazy?

00:11:47.958 --> 00:11:52.504
No one knows where,
when or how man first landed on the moon.

00:11:52.629 --> 00:11:55.591
- I do.
- But our fungineers think

00:11:55.674 --> 00:11:58.427
It might have happened
something like this.

00:11:59.052 --> 00:12:01.305
We're whalers on the moon

00:12:01.388 --> 00:12:03.390
We carry a harpoon

00:12:03.765 --> 00:12:06.018
But there ain't no whales
so we tell tall tales

00:12:06.226 --> 00:12:08.061
And sing a whaling tune

00:12:08.187 --> 00:12:10.355
That's not how it happened.

00:12:10.439 --> 00:12:13.150
Oh, really? I don't see you
with a fungineering degree.

00:12:13.275 --> 00:12:14.776
This is stupid.

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:16.862
I'm taking this thing
out to the real moon.

00:12:16.945 --> 00:12:19.114
Fry, no. This is my first mission

00:12:19.198 --> 00:12:21.533
and I'm not going to let us
get in any trouble.

00:12:21.617 --> 00:12:23.243
Besides, the car's on a track.

00:12:23.327 --> 00:12:24.328
Not for long.

00:12:27.331 --> 00:12:28.373
We're whalers...

00:12:28.457 --> 00:12:29.875
Oh! Ow!

00:12:29.958 --> 00:12:32.294
I died doing what I loved.

00:12:33.086 --> 00:12:35.255
Okay, you're on the surface.

00:12:35.339 --> 00:12:36.673
Now, I'll give you ten minutes.

00:12:36.757 --> 00:12:38.634
then you'll get bored, turn around

00:12:38.717 --> 00:12:40.844
and apologize for being such a jerk.

00:12:40.928 --> 00:12:42.513
- Agreed?
- Agreed.

00:12:42.721 --> 00:12:44.139
Yee-ha!

00:12:45.974 --> 00:12:47.726
Yeah! Crank up the radio!

00:12:48.227 --> 00:12:50.103
We're whalers on the...

00:12:50.896 --> 00:12:52.481
Yee-ha!

00:12:55.909 --> 00:12:58.412
Time's up.
Make a U-turn at the next crater.

00:12:58.495 --> 00:12:59.496
No, not yet.

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:01.832
How about we go look
for the original moon landing site?

00:13:01.915 --> 00:13:04.209
That's crazy.
It's been lost for centuries.

00:13:04.293 --> 00:13:06.253
Well, I'm feeling lucky.

00:13:06.336 --> 00:13:07.462
Ooh.

00:13:12.551 --> 00:13:15.262
Uh... I'm ready to go back now.

00:13:18.473 --> 00:13:21.101
We're going to die!
It's every man for himself!

00:13:21.476 --> 00:13:22.477
Help me, Leela!

00:13:27.441 --> 00:13:29.276
Whoo!

00:13:33.697 --> 00:13:34.698
You did it.

00:13:34.781 --> 00:13:35.782
We're safe.

00:13:36.116 --> 00:13:38.035
No. Now we're going to die.

00:13:39.286 --> 00:13:41.079
It's every man for himself!

00:13:45.792 --> 00:13:48.128
Hey, look what I won
from a tourist's pocket.

00:13:48.211 --> 00:13:50.255
Shut up. You're distracting me.

00:13:50.505 --> 00:13:52.549
Come on, it's just like making love.

00:13:52.633 --> 00:13:56.345
You know, left, down,
rotate 62 degrees

00:13:56.428 --> 00:13:57.721
Engage rotor.

00:13:57.804 --> 00:13:59.765
I know how to make love.

00:14:02.226 --> 00:14:03.560
Here, let me do it.

00:14:08.607 --> 00:14:10.817
Oh, lousy arm must be rigged.

00:14:12.736 --> 00:14:14.029
That's her, officers.

00:14:14.112 --> 00:14:16.573
That's the woman
who programmed me for evil.

00:14:22.537 --> 00:14:27.000
Yeah, well, I'm going to go
build my own theme park

00:14:27.084 --> 00:14:29.086
With blackjack and hookers.

00:14:29.169 --> 00:14:31.421
In fact, forget the park.

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:38.011
I'm sorry, Leela.

00:14:38.095 --> 00:14:39.721
I can't go on any further.

00:14:39.805 --> 00:14:42.349
Just leave me to die
in that barn over there.

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:50.774
Oh, thank God.

00:14:52.901 --> 00:14:54.278
Trespassers, eh?

00:14:54.486 --> 00:14:56.780
No, sir. We're amusement park patrons.

00:14:56.947 --> 00:14:59.658
Ooh, that's a wicked, sinful place.

00:14:59.908 --> 00:15:02.869
Tilt-a-whirl's okay,
but the rest is mighty wicked.

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:05.080
Our car broke down
and we're out of oxygen.

00:15:05.163 --> 00:15:06.331
Can we borrow some?

00:15:06.415 --> 00:15:11.086
"Borry?" Looky here, city girl,
oxygen don't grow on trees.

00:15:11.253 --> 00:15:14.423
You'll have to earn it doing chores
on my hydroponic farm.

00:15:14.506 --> 00:15:17.551
You can go back to your precious
theme park at sunup.

00:15:17.843 --> 00:15:20.137
I guess we could do chores
for a few hours.

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:22.681
Fry, night lasts two weeks on the moon.

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:26.018
Yep. Drops down to minus 173.

00:15:26.184 --> 00:15:27.936
Fahrenheit or Celsius?

00:15:28.103 --> 00:15:29.897
First one, then the other.

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:34.026
And them space suits ain't a-heated
so you ain't going nowhere till sunrise.

00:15:34.109 --> 00:15:35.444
You can sleep in the barn.

00:15:35.611 --> 00:15:37.821
Just don't be a-touchin'

00:15:37.905 --> 00:15:40.991
my three beautiful
robot daughters, you hear?

00:15:41.283 --> 00:15:42.659
Robot daughters?

00:15:42.951 --> 00:15:44.661
This here's Lulabelle 7...

00:15:44.745 --> 00:15:46.079
Yoo-hoo.

00:15:46.163 --> 00:15:48.206
Daisy Mae 128-K...

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:49.917
Yoo-hoo.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.710
And the Crushinator.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:55.088
Yoo-hoo.

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:56.673
Whoa!

00:15:57.174 --> 00:15:59.968
I told you to turn around
and go back to the park.

00:16:00.219 --> 00:16:02.596
But, oh, no.
The park was too phony.

00:16:02.679 --> 00:16:04.223
We had to see the real moon.

00:16:04.389 --> 00:16:05.557
And it was great.

00:16:05.641 --> 00:16:07.226
We got to see craters and rocks

00:16:07.309 --> 00:16:09.895
and that one incredible rock
that looked like a crater

00:16:09.978 --> 00:16:11.063
And... And these fellas.

00:16:13.232 --> 00:16:15.651
Fry, face it, the moon is a dump.

00:16:15.734 --> 00:16:17.778
It's a boring dried-up wasteland.

00:16:17.861 --> 00:16:19.863
And the only reason
anybody ever comes here

00:16:19.947 --> 00:16:22.115
is for the tacky
little amusement park.

00:16:22.199 --> 00:16:23.533
Can't you just accept that?

00:16:23.617 --> 00:16:25.953
I guess I can't.

00:16:27.663 --> 00:16:30.666
I'll learn you to sleep
with my robot daughters.

00:16:32.417 --> 00:16:35.003
He'll never find me in here.

00:16:35.212 --> 00:16:36.213
Bender?

00:16:36.338 --> 00:16:39.716
Ugh. Bender, you didn't touch
the Crushinator, did you?

00:16:40.259 --> 00:16:43.512
Of course not. A lady that fine
you got to romance first.

00:16:56.149 --> 00:16:57.484
Oh, no, you don't.

00:16:57.568 --> 00:16:58.902
Come here, Crushinator.

00:16:58.986 --> 00:17:00.779
Yes, Pa.

00:17:18.171 --> 00:17:19.756
- It's too low!
- Hang on.

00:17:19.881 --> 00:17:21.258
Hang on. Jump!

00:17:26.763 --> 00:17:28.098
Hold on to your helmet.

00:17:28.307 --> 00:17:29.933
Whoa!

00:17:35.606 --> 00:17:36.857
- Yes!
- Oh, boy.

00:17:41.778 --> 00:17:44.823
Goldurn it, Crushinator, jump!

00:17:44.907 --> 00:17:48.410
No, Pa. I love him.

00:17:49.202 --> 00:17:51.455
Oh!

00:17:52.915 --> 00:17:55.876
Hey, cool. Dark side of the moon.

00:17:56.043 --> 00:17:57.628
Nightfall's coming.

00:17:59.838 --> 00:18:01.423
Hurry, before we freeze.

00:18:01.673 --> 00:18:03.592
What do you mean we, mammal?

00:18:11.308 --> 00:18:12.309
Oh, dear.

00:18:12.392 --> 00:18:14.645
I really ought to do something.

00:18:14.728 --> 00:18:17.773
But I'm already in my pajamas.

00:18:23.195 --> 00:18:24.821
We can't outrun it forever.

00:18:25.614 --> 00:18:27.658
Over there. Look!

00:18:28.283 --> 00:18:29.701
It's the moon landing site.

00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:30.994
We found it.

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:37.918
Quick, get in.

00:18:39.127 --> 00:18:42.005
It's that flag from MTV.

00:18:42.089 --> 00:18:44.341
And Neil Armstrong's footprint.

00:18:45.676 --> 00:18:47.344
Hey, my foot's bigger.

00:18:47.719 --> 00:18:50.639
Leela, isn't this the greatest
thing you've ever seen?

00:18:50.973 --> 00:18:52.432
Fry, look around.

00:18:52.558 --> 00:18:56.228
It's just a crummy plastic flag
and a dead man's tracks in the dust.

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:02.609
Now, get in here before you freeze.

00:19:12.369 --> 00:19:14.705
Oh, no room for Bender, huh?

00:19:14.788 --> 00:19:17.749
Fine, I'll go build my own lunar lander

00:19:17.833 --> 00:19:20.544
With blackjack and hookers.

00:19:20.627 --> 00:19:23.880
In fact, forget the lunar lander
and the blackjack.

00:19:23.964 --> 00:19:25.674
Ah, screw the whole thing.

00:19:26.174 --> 00:19:28.093
Well, if the oxygen holds out,

00:19:28.176 --> 00:19:30.178
we might live long enough
to starve to death.

00:19:30.429 --> 00:19:34.099
Look, Leela, I'm sorry.
I never should have dragged you out here.

00:19:34.308 --> 00:19:36.310
That's right. You shouldn't have.

00:19:36.393 --> 00:19:38.520
I still don't get
what the big attraction is.

00:19:39.187 --> 00:19:41.565
I never told anybody this

00:19:41.648 --> 00:19:44.359
but a thousand years ago,
I used to look up at the moon

00:19:44.443 --> 00:19:46.111
and dream about being an astronaut.

00:19:46.194 --> 00:19:49.406
I just didn't have the grades
or the physical endurance.

00:19:49.489 --> 00:19:50.657
Plus, I threw up a lot

00:19:50.741 --> 00:19:52.618
and nobody likes
spending a week with me.

00:19:52.701 --> 00:19:54.453
A week would be a little much.

00:19:54.661 --> 00:19:58.373
The moon was like this awesome,
romantic, mysterious thing

00:19:58.457 --> 00:20:01.043
hanging up there in the sky
where you could never reach it

00:20:01.126 --> 00:20:02.920
no matter how much you wanted to.

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:05.672
But you're right.

00:20:05.756 --> 00:20:08.759
Once you're actually here,
it's just a big dull rock.

00:20:08.842 --> 00:20:11.595
I guess I just wanted you
to see it through my eyes

00:20:11.803 --> 00:20:13.013
The way I used to.

00:20:17.684 --> 00:20:19.102
Fry, look.

00:20:20.771 --> 00:20:22.898
It really is beautiful.

00:20:23.315 --> 00:20:25.609
I don't know why
I never noticed before.

00:20:34.993 --> 00:20:38.288
Had to come back
for the Crushinator, eh, robot?

00:20:38.372 --> 00:20:40.207
Well, I got you this time.

00:20:49.508 --> 00:20:51.593
It's Amy. We're saved.

00:20:51.843 --> 00:20:53.053
Amy?

00:20:53.136 --> 00:20:55.597
Where'd she learn to operate
the controls like that?

00:21:04.114 --> 00:21:05.324
Not the magnet.

00:21:05.407 --> 00:21:08.660
No! No! No!

00:21:08.744 --> 00:21:09.828
Uh-oh.

00:21:12.497 --> 00:21:15.834
She'll be coming around
the mountain when she comes

00:21:15.917 --> 00:21:18.587
She'll be coming around
the mountain when she comes

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:19.880
I'll kill you, Amy!

00:21:19.963 --> 00:21:21.465
She'll be coming around the mountain

00:21:21.548 --> 00:21:23.133
She'll be coming around
the mountain, she'll be...

00:21:28.221 --> 00:21:29.431
Ah, dang it.

00:21:36.521 --> 00:21:41.026
She'll be riding six
white horses when she comes

00:21:41.109 --> 00:21:43.320
She'll be riding six
whitehorses when she comes

00:21:43.403 --> 00:21:44.446
Hey, I'm pretty good.

00:21:44.529 --> 00:21:46.281
She'll be riding
six white horses

00:21:46.365 --> 00:21:48.408
So, Fry, was the real moon

00:21:48.492 --> 00:21:51.036
anything like the moon
you used to dream about?

00:21:51.119 --> 00:21:53.163
Uh... Close enough.

00:21:54.498 --> 00:21:58.043
Well, I'll shoot her
with my ray-gun when she comes

00:21:58.377 --> 00:22:01.546
Yes, I'll shoot her
with my ray-gun when she comes

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:04.925
Yes, I'll shoot her with my ray-gun
Oh, I'llshoot her with my ray-gun

00:22:05.008 --> 00:22:08.011
Yes, I'll shoot her withmy ray-gun
when she comes, when she comes

00:22:08.095 --> 00:22:11.014
I'll be blasting
all the humans in the world

00:22:11.098 --> 00:22:14.184
I'll be blasting
all the humans in the world

00:22:14.268 --> 00:22:17.688
I'll be blasting all the humans
I'll be blasting all the humans

00:22:17.771 --> 00:22:19.898
I'll be blasting
all the humans in the world

00:22:19.942 --> 00:22:21.151
In the world

00:22:21.316 --> 00:22:24.278
One more time!